  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening regional architecture</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia has supported the University of the South Pacific (USP), the region&#x2019;s pre-eminent and largest tertiary education provider and a designated Council of Regional Organisations of the Pacific (CROP) agency, since its establishment in 1968. Our partnership with USP provides an important platform for high level, strategic dialogue on tertiary education and regionalism in the Pacific, including supporting the priority needs of Pacific island countries (PICs) through delivery of the Pacific Regional Education Framework (PacREF). In 2024, USP delivered quality tertiary education services to 25,279 students across 14 campuses, and graduated 4,277 students. It also hosted 444 New Colombo Plan scholars and mobility grants students at the Laucala Campus in Suva. USP co-hosted the Conference of Pacific Education Ministers (CPEM) in Papua New Guinea in March 2025, and continues to develop a range of resources to support the region&#x2019;s teachers and educators through the delivery of PacREF activities including assistance with education policy and planning and the establishment of the regional Learning Hub, Waka Moana, providing online educational resources for teachers.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening regional architecture</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia has supported the University of the South Pacific (USP), the region&#x2019;s pre-eminent tertiary education provider and Council of Regional Organisations of the Pacific (CROP) agency, since its establishment.  In 2023, USP delivered quality tertiary education services to 26,777 students across 14 campuses.  Australia&#x2019;s partnership with USP provides a platform for high-level strategic dialogue, including around the Pacific Regional Education Framework, and through USP&#x2019;s co-hosting the Conference of Pacific Education Ministers in New Zealand in 2023.  In 2023, we broadened our partnership to support USP&#x2019;s Pacific TAFE to expand its skills and training offerings to other regional campuses.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia invests in the University of the South Pacific (USP), an established regional organisation co-owned by 12 member countries. Our partnership with USP ($86m, 2019-25) strengthens the University as a regional public good delivering tertiary education services to over 15,000 students annually.  Australia&#x2019;s representatives on USP Council and University Grants Committee provide advice on university governance and reforms. In 2023 USP co-hosted the Conference of Pacific Education Ministers, where ministers reaffirmed their support for the Pacific Regional Education Framework (PacREF). USP is an implementing agency for the PacREF, the region&#x2019;s key education reform agenda.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
